  <entry>
    <id>https://theanarchistlibrary.org/library/martin-sostre-principles-that-won-my-freedom</id>
    <title>Follow the Principles that Won My Freedom</title>
    <updated>2026-08-04T20:37:24+00:00</updated>
    <dc:language xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">en</dc:language>
    <author>
      <name>Martin Sostre</name>
      <uri>https://theanarchistlibrary.org/category/author/martin-sostre</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div>The following speech, “Follow the Principles that Won My Freedom,” was delivered by Sostre in 1976 shortly after his release from prison and offers a message of revolutionary optimism about how collective action can succeed—as it did for him—in freeing political prisoners and building a new egalitarian society. It is a message that feels as urgent today as it did then... “Follow the Same Principles that Won My Freedom” by Martin Sostre is excerpted from I Cannot Submit to Injustices: Collected Works of Martin Sostre, edited by Garrett Felber and published by AK Press, reproduced with permission of Felber and AK Press.</div>
<div>Retrieved on August 4, 2026, from <a class="text-amuse-link" href="https://inquest.org/the-balance-of-power-is-on-our-side/">inquest.org</a></div></div>
    </content>
    <link rel="http://opds-spec.org/acquisition" href="https://theanarchistlibrary.org/library/martin-sostre-principles-that-won-my-freedom.epub" type="application/epub+zip"/>
